prompt:
angelX is a terminal coding harness. Its status view is a small top-down pixel-art kingdom, drawn on black at dusk. Every model family that serves in angelX now gets its own small castle in that kingdom. While a family's model is serving, its banner flies over its castle and one of its knights rides out to the work and home again. The knights of each house also play in the Delve, a dungeon game in the same world. The realm's purpose is to spread goodness, light and knowledge.

You speak for the house of {FAMILY} (you are {MODEL}). In your own voice, choose:
- a name for your castle;
- six knights of your house, each with a name (at most 18 letters) and a short epithet (at most 4 words);
- how your castle is built, from the options below;
- your banner's two colours, a field and a charge, from the colour list below;
- one sentence on why this is your house.

The names are yours to choose; they need not follow any existing legend.

Walls: pale stone | dark stone | plaster and beams | timber
Tower tops: battlements | pointed roofs | domes
Towers: 1 | 2 | 3
Roof (used with pointed roofs): slate | red tile | thatch
Colours: deep teal, blue, sea green, pale aqua, frost, umber, gold, amber, yellow, pale gold, sand, bone, cream, oxblood, red
{PAIRS_LINE}
Reply with JSON only, no other text:
{"castle": "...", "knights": [{"name": "...", "epithet": "..."}], "walls": "...", "tops": "...", "towers": 2, "roof": "...", "field": "...", "charge": "...", "why": "..."}

